From: Fransis <arcadematicas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: adreno a8xx: force GX GDSC collapse before CX in recovery

On SM8750 (Adreno 830) the GX GDSC lives in the separate gxclkctl domain and
feeds the shader cores + the CX GDSC power dependency.  After a GMU hang the
firmware leaves GX voted on in HW (RPMH), so CX cannot collapse while GX is
up.  The recovery deadlocks ("cx gdsc didn't collapse") and the next hw_init
times out on "GMU OOB GPU_SET" -- which on gamescope/turnip surfaces as
VkDeviceLost (VkResult -4) in the compositor.

Fix: collapse GX before CX in a8xx_recover(), mirroring a6xx_gmu_gxpd_put()
(unconditional, since gx_is_on() reads false while the GMU is hung).

Tested on the AYN Odin 3 (pocknix-os, kernel 7.1.0): gamescope compositor no
longer loses the device (VkDeviceLost count 0).

NOTE: the original version of this file was a hand-written diff with a fake
index line and wrong hunk counts, so it never applied. Regenerated 15/09/2026
against linux-7.2 + the full sm8750 patch stack.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
@@ -903,6 +903,21 @@
 	 * runtime suspend cb
 	 */
 	gpu->active_submits = 0;
+	/*
+	 * A8xx (SM8750/Adreno 830): the GX GDSC lives in the separate gxclkctl
+	 * domain and feeds the shader cores + the CX GDSC power dependency.
+	 * On a GMU hang the firmware leaves GX voted on in HW (RPMH), so CX
+	 * cannot collapse while GX is up -> recovery deadlocks ("cx gdsc
+	 * didn't collapse"), and the next hw_init times out on "GMU OOB GPU_SET".
+	 * Force GX collapse BEFORE CX (mirrors a6xx_gmu_gxpd_put, unconditional
+	 * since gx_is_on() reads false while the GMU is hung).
+	 */
+	if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(gmu->gxpd)) {
+		pm_runtime_get_sync(gmu->gxpd);
+		dev_pm_genpd_synced_poweroff(gmu->gxpd);
+		pm_runtime_put_sync(gmu->gxpd);
+	}
+
 
 	reinit_completion(&gmu->pd_gate);
 	dev_pm_genpd_add_notifier(gmu->cxpd, &gmu->pd_nb);
